{
 "definitions": "Descriptive group comparisons for the skill references, from the campaign analysis. Writes analysis/output/comparisons.json.\n\n  python3 analysis/compare_groups.py [build-inputs/tables] [--classification FILE]\n\nImpressions in the dataset are unique per day, so a returning visitor counts once per day. Repeatable actions\n(daily bonus, loyalty, timed bonus) and long runs inflate impressions and depress contestants per impression.\nConversion comparisons therefore use a CLEAN subset: campaigns with no repeatable action and a run of 14 days\nor less. Every figure is a median and describes what organizers chose. Every campaign is in the ordinary frame\nfrom frame.py, 1,000 or more contestants, and every published group needs five distinct organizers. Verticals\nfold the homepage-label industry into the ten names the skill references already use, industry rows carry the\nlabel as reported.",
